DBC code and works based on it for noncommercial purposes only.

The two files named above are therefore excluded from the MIT grant in the
repository's root LICENSE. They are research code: they were written to check
Trucee's solvency claims against DBC's rounding, and they are for research use
only. Do not use them, or anything derived from them, for commercial purposes.

Every sim/ file not named above (the router model zero_pvp.py, the fuzz and
sniper scripts, the replay and export tools, and the tests) is Trucee's own
work under the MIT licence in the root LICENSE. Those files only import and
call functions from the two files above; they copy none of DBC's code.

The rest of the repository is Trucee code under the MIT licence in the root
